	(text "XOUT is the output from\nthe crystal (so it's an\ninput to the MCU)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 203.2 133.858 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.635 0.635)
			)
		)
		(uuid "04734507-4d36-40b2-b4ec-0f6b191390aa")
	)
	(text "tells receptacle to\nallow power to go\nthrough to power \nthe board"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 38.608 77.978 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.635 0.635)
			)
		)
		(uuid "20d96f56-1f1e-444d-a7eb-d7f04b6a978c")
	)
	(text "look at the rp2040 data sheet\nthere's eight IO VDD pins so we \nput in eight 0.1uF decoupling capacitors,\nwith one 1uF cap because we're \nwiring the entire 3.3V line and need\nto smooth out the larger ripples"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 156.718 24.638 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.635 0.635)
			)
		)
		(uuid "20db5a90-9e08-406c-a81a-530d49adb9b6")
	)
	(text "all the input/outputs\nare bidirectional"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 187.198 110.744 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.635 0.635)
			)
		)
		(uuid "2e5043ab-5c6c-4e9d-8eeb-9e4c50f4aa48")
	)
	(text "XIN is an output from\nthe MCU (so it's an\noutput from the MCU)\nthat helps the crystal\noscillate properly"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 195.58 119.888 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.635 0.635)
			)
		)
		(uuid "40036de5-5532-4910-aaaf-dc478f40bca1")
	)
	(text "capacitors on each \nside of the LDO\nfor input/output"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 99.568 85.344 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.635 0.635)
			)
		)
		(uuid "4673b40d-da83-4849-b8fa-9e5bcfbdee04")
	)
	(text "10k resistor is \njust standard shit"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 50.546 160.274 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.635 0.635)
			)
		)
		(uuid "4cdcad9a-e94e-49f2-a1c6-75662dff39d9")
	)
	(text "pullup to 3.3V is important since\nQSPI will usually show up as 3.3V\nto flash memory, bu during bootup,\nyou ca'nt guarantee it will since\npin isn't active. thus, you might\nhave weird things happen with ur\nboard"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 37.592 146.304 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.381 0.381)
			)
		)
		(uuid "5df7f1cf-e2a6-4c22-bcfc-2ab1ccdc22c6")
	)
	(text "5V power input line"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 64.77 62.484 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.635 0.635)
			)
		)
		(uuid "60384c09-6da8-469b-8384-cb498c989514")
	)
	(text "MOSI - Master output, slave input\nMISO - Master input, slave output\nSCLK - Clock signal (remember that oscillator we added to our board, this will basically do that for other devices)\nSS/CS - Slave select, let's you choose what device you're communicating with"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 44.196 131.826 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.381 0.381)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "6c119631-28f3-4419-8336-9216540bfe24")
	)
	(text "add a 100nF decoupling capacitor\nto the VCC line to filter high-freq\nnoise"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 75.184 149.098 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.635 0.635)
			)
		)
		(uuid "6da074ff-286d-4fae-b55e-230a87d06b09")
	)
	(text "quad spi has 4 IO pins so it's\n4x as fast as SPI (which is ideal\nfor flash memory) (except it also\ntakes more pins so it's not widely\nused)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 85.852 136.652 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.635 0.635)
			)
		)
		(uuid "6e1eda12-12ee-4969-8ca6-acc8bc0c3d63")
	)
	(text "RP2040 pinout diagram & pin\nexplanations & descriptions\non page 12 of \nhttps://pip-assets.raspberrypi.com/\ncategories/814-rp2040/documents/\nRP-008371-DS-1-rp2040-datasheet.pdf"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 261.366 22.098 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "728c5d63-30c2-4d48-8469-6989024523b1")
	)
	(text "this is basically: if the QSPI SS pin\nsees a 0 or GND when booting up, it'll\ngo into BOOTSEL, where it'll appear as\na USB device on our computer so we can\ncopy code onto it to set it up"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 28.448 172.974 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.635 0.635)
			)
		)
		(uuid "8147c043-a729-4ff8-a8c7-2d718d995d00")
	)
	(text "receptacle because a plug\nwould need to plug into ur \nlaptop instead of having a \ncable plug into it ykyk"
